---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const sections = [['scope','Scope'],['data','Data we access'],['use','How data is used'],['sharing','Services & sharing'],['storage','Storage & retention'],['control','Your choices'],['contact','Contact']];
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy policy — Agoca Labs" description="How Agoca Labs Email Manager accesses, processes, stores, and shares data from Gmail, Google Sheets, and Telegram.">
<div class="policy-header wrap"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY & DATA</p><h1>Your data.<br />A clear explanation.</h1><p class="policy-date">Privacy policy · Effective September 6, 2026</p><p>This policy describes the Agoca Labs website and the personal Email Manager automation, including its Morning Brief and Telegram rule-update features.</p></div>
<div class="policy-layout wrap"><nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">{sections.map(([id,label])=><a href={'#'+id}>{label}</a>)}</nav><article class="policy-content">
<section id="scope"><h2>01. Who this policy covers</h2><p>Agoca Labs is an independent project operated by Agoca. Email Manager is currently used for personal automation with accounts authorized by its operator. This website provides information about the project; it does not offer public registration or collect Google account credentials.</p><p>This policy covers information accessed through connected Google accounts, messages exchanged with the Telegram bot, and technical information associated with visiting this website.</p></section>
<section id="data"><h2>02. Data we access</h2><ul><li><strong>Gmail:</strong> selected message content and metadata, including sender, subject, date, message identifiers, and read status, to classify email and prepare summaries.</li><li><strong>Google Sheets:</strong> classification rules and preferences in the connected rules spreadsheet. Confirmed rule updates are written back to that spreadsheet.</li><li><strong>Telegram:</strong> chat identifiers, messages, replies, and conversational context needed to respond to requests and update rules.</li><li><strong>Connection information:</strong> OAuth access and refresh tokens needed to use authorized Google services. Google handles account sign-in; the automation does not need your Google password.</li><li><strong>Website requests:</strong> the hosting provider may process IP addresses, browser information, request timestamps, and security or diagnostic logs to deliver and protect the website.</li></ul></section>
<section id="use"><h2>03. What we do with it</h2><p>Email Manager analyzes selected email using locally hosted AI models, applies the configured rules, and prepares a brief highlighting important messages and useful updates. It sends that brief to the configured Telegram chat. Configured workflows may also mark processed Gmail messages as read.</p><p>Telegram conversations help interpret rule-change requests. Confirmed updates are saved in Google Sheets for later runs. Workflow execution records may contain input messages, model outputs, and error details used to operate and troubleshoot the automation.</p><p>Google user data is not sold, used for advertising, or used to train general-purpose AI models. Local model inference produces classifications and summaries; it does not train the underlying models.</p><p class="callout">Agoca Labs' use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p></section>
<section id="sharing"><h2>04. Where information goes</h2><p>Local AI processing does not mean every part of the workflow stays on one device. These services support the features described above:</p><ul><li><strong>Google</strong> stores the original Gmail messages and connected Google Sheets data and provides the authorized APIs.</li><li><strong>The operator's server</strong> runs n8n and Ollama to coordinate workflows and analyze messages.</li><li><strong>Telegram</strong> receives the generated brief, which may contain email-derived information, and processes bot conversations.</li><li><strong>ngrok</strong> provides the HTTPS tunnel for incoming bot messages and access to the automation interface; traffic through that tunnel is processed by ngrok.</li><li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this public informational website and may process website request and security logs. The site itself does not display private inbox data.</li></ul><p>Service providers handle information under their own applicable terms and privacy policies. Data is shared as needed to deliver the configured features, or where required by law or necessary to address security incidents.</p></section>
<section id="storage"><h2>05. Storage, retention & security</h2><p>The automation stores configuration, connection tokens, and workflow execution data on the operator's server. n8n encrypts saved credentials using its instance encryption key. This does not mean all workflow execution content is encrypted at rest.</p><p>Retention depends on configured execution-history settings and manual cleanup. There is currently no single automatic deletion period across all connected services. Rules remain in Google Sheets until edited or removed; messages and briefs remain in Gmail or Telegram according to those services' settings and deletion actions.</p><p>Copies in backups, if backups are enabled, may remain until those backups are removed or expire. Revoking account access prevents future authorized access but does not automatically delete existing messages, execution records, or backups.</p><p>Access controls and HTTPS on public endpoints help protect information. No system can guarantee absolute security. Avoid including information in rule requests that is unnecessary for the automation.</p></section>
<section id="control"><h2>06. Your choices</h2><p>You can revoke Google access through your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google Account connections</a>. The operator can also disconnect credentials, stop workflows, delete execution history, and remove stored configuration.</p><p>Original Gmail messages, Google Sheets entries, and Telegram conversations must be managed in their respective services. For questions about access or removal of information held by the automation, contact the operator using the address below.</p><p>This website does not add advertising trackers, analytics scripts, or a contact form. Hosting and security services may still process technical request information.</p></section>
<section id="contact"><h2>07. Contact & policy updates</h2><p>For privacy questions or data-removal requests, email <a href="mailto:agomezcasarez@gmail.com">agomezcasarez@gmail.com</a>.</p><p>This policy will be updated when the project changes how it handles information. The effective date above identifies the current version. Material new uses of connected Google data will be disclosed, and additional consent will be requested where required.</p></section>
</article></div></SiteLayout>
